<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112951" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλάζ-ιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>full of knots</i> or
				<i>clots,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σπέρμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Steph.
					<u>in Hp.</u>
					2.479D.
				</span></i>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> epith. of Zeus, <i>god
				of hail,</i> at Cyzicus, <i><span class="en">
				<u>JHS</u>
				24.21
			</span></i>; of Apollo at Thebes, <i><span class="en">
				Procl.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
				<u>Bibl.</u>
				p.321
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			Subst., name of a precious stone, <i>resembling a
				hailstone,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>L.</u>
				758
			</span></i>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλαζίας.</span></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
